1
00:00:07,504 --> 00:00:09,494
Dobato. What are you up to now?

2
00:00:09,874 --> 00:00:12,864
I'm making some decorations
with this pretty paper.

3
00:00:13,344 --> 00:00:15,914
Isn't that the paper the landlady gave you?

4
00:00:15,914 --> 00:00:20,284
Yes, Ms. Chitose gave it to me
to take to the kindergarten.

5
00:00:20,284 --> 00:00:22,684
She said she won a whole bunch of
them at the shopping district.

6
00:00:22,884 --> 00:00:26,684
I'm going to make lots of decorations like
these to put on the windows and walls.

7
00:00:27,094 --> 00:00:29,524
Do you think that will make everyone happy?!

8
00:00:30,124 --> 00:00:32,184
I think they'll feel stifled.

9
00:00:34,134 --> 00:00:36,124
Why don't I tell you something worthwhile?

10
00:00:36,664 --> 00:00:41,264
That paper is called origami, and origami is
normally used and enjoyed as folding paper.

11
00:00:41,374 --> 00:00:42,424
What?!

12
00:00:44,274 --> 00:00:47,474
Wh... What should I do?! Ioryogi-san?

13
00:00:47,574 --> 00:00:52,384
I can't... I can't put it back the
way it was! Ioryogi-san...

14
00:00:52,384 --> 00:00:53,974
You cut it up already.

15
00:00:54,714 --> 00:00:56,814
How do you expect to put it back together?!

16
00:01:03,664 --> 00:01:06,794
Kobato.

17
00:01:06,794 --> 00:01:09,634
Kobato.
What should I do?

18
00:01:09,634 --> 00:01:14,034
Kobato.
Even the most obvious of things

19
00:01:14,934 --> 00:01:18,244
Are always such a challenge

20
00:01:18,244 --> 00:01:21,014
I want to laugh when I'm happy

21
00:01:21,014 --> 00:01:25,314
And sing whenever I want

22
00:01:25,884 --> 00:01:28,314
Is all

23
00:01:29,614 --> 00:01:33,984
They say my dreams will come true someday

24
00:01:34,424 --> 00:01:37,694
But when will "someday" come?

25
00:01:37,694 --> 00:01:41,184
I can't wait forever

26
00:01:41,334 --> 00:01:47,104
On "1, 2, 3!" I'll spread open my arms

27
00:01:47,104 --> 00:01:52,304
And let the light gather around me

28
00:01:52,304 --> 00:01:55,144
Where is it?

29
00:01:55,144 --> 00:01:58,484
Please tell me what I can do

30
00:01:58,484 --> 00:02:01,314
I make the most of getting hurt

31
00:02:01,314 --> 00:02:04,224
And run with all my might

32
00:02:04,224 --> 00:02:08,194
Despite how many dozens of times I fall

33
00:02:08,194 --> 00:02:11,224
And start crying

34
00:02:11,224 --> 00:02:15,254
I surprise myself

35
00:02:15,734 --> 00:02:19,894
In how much I believe in tomorrow

36
00:02:29,644 --> 00:02:33,674
...Hidden Prayer.

37
00:02:45,494 --> 00:02:46,624
Thanks.

38
00:02:46,834 --> 00:02:48,194
Ms. Sayaka.

39
00:02:49,094 --> 00:02:53,034
You haven't been getting enough
sleep, have you? You look tired.

40
00:02:53,034 --> 00:02:54,194
Now, now.

41
00:02:54,934 --> 00:02:57,634
You don't tell women that they look tired.

42
00:02:57,904 --> 00:02:58,934
You could hurt their feelings.

43
00:02:59,144 --> 00:03:00,544
I'm not joking!

44
00:03:03,814 --> 00:03:05,944
I'll leave this at the office.

45
00:03:07,514 --> 00:03:08,674
Thank you.

46
00:03:17,294 --> 00:03:19,484
U-Um... Ms. Sayaka.

47
00:03:19,794 --> 00:03:20,764
Oh?

48
00:03:20,894 --> 00:03:22,194
Kobato.

49
00:03:22,494 --> 00:03:24,264
I-I'm sorry!

50
00:03:24,364 --> 00:03:25,994
What is it, all of a sudden?

51
00:03:26,534 --> 00:03:30,934
Um... Ms. Chisato gave me these to give
to everyone at the kindergarten.

52
00:03:32,874 --> 00:03:35,674
Oh, origami. So much of it.

53
00:03:35,944 --> 00:03:44,254
Actually there was more, but... I didn't know
that origami was for folding so I messed it up.

54
00:03:44,424 --> 00:03:46,044
I'm really sorry!

55
00:03:52,764 --> 00:03:53,924
Ms. Sayaka?

56
00:03:56,864 --> 00:03:59,594
Ms. Sayaka! Ms. Sayaka!

57
00:04:00,034 --> 00:04:02,434
Fujimoto! Fujimoto!

58
00:04:02,904 --> 00:04:03,904
What is it?

59
00:04:03,904 --> 00:04:05,534
It's Ms. Sayaka!

60
00:04:08,974 --> 00:04:10,014
I'm okay.

61
00:04:10,014 --> 00:04:11,574
Let's get you to the hospital right away.

62
00:04:12,314 --> 00:04:13,614
I'm all right.

63
00:04:13,614 --> 00:04:16,084
You are not all right! Look at you!

64
00:04:16,554 --> 00:04:20,814
Really. I just need a little rest... and I'll be fine.

65
00:04:21,494 --> 00:04:24,854
I know a doctor! I'll go and get him right away!

66
00:04:32,264 --> 00:04:33,394
Kobato?

67
00:04:33,774 --> 00:04:35,964
Kobato, where are you going?

68
00:04:50,084 --> 00:04:51,414
Hello?!

69
00:04:51,924 --> 00:04:54,254
Hello, excuse me! Open the door please!

70
00:04:55,524 --> 00:04:57,994
Will you open the door please? Please!

71
00:04:59,464 --> 00:05:00,864
Kobato?

72
00:05:00,864 --> 00:05:02,054
What's the matter?

73
00:05:02,294 --> 00:05:03,764
Um! Where's Shuichiro?

74
00:05:06,804 --> 00:05:09,204
Please help us. Ms. Sayaka...!

75
00:05:09,304 --> 00:05:10,534
Please!

76
00:05:28,494 --> 00:05:30,614
What's wrong with Ms. Sayaka?

77
00:05:31,464 --> 00:05:33,524
Nothing you have to worry about.

78
00:05:40,274 --> 00:05:41,394
How is she?

79
00:05:41,474 --> 00:05:45,734
She's suffering from fatigue and
gastritis due to lack of sleep.

80
00:05:46,774 --> 00:05:47,834
I see.

81
00:05:49,414 --> 00:05:50,934
I'll prescribe some medication later.

82
00:05:51,644 --> 00:05:55,444
After she's had some rest and feels settled,
feed her something that digests well.

83
00:05:55,984 --> 00:05:59,284
Okay. Thank you for coming
at such short notice.

84
00:05:59,584 --> 00:06:02,794
No worries. Good thing it was my day off.

85
00:06:02,794 --> 00:06:04,024
Uh, um...

86
00:06:04,324 --> 00:06:06,654
Is Ms. Sayaka going to be okay?

87
00:06:08,034 --> 00:06:12,554
If she keeps this up, she'll eventually
end up in much worse condition.

88
00:06:14,334 --> 00:06:16,634
Don't pass it off as simple fatigue.

89
00:06:17,974 --> 00:06:20,104
Please tell her what I just said.

90
00:06:20,814 --> 00:06:22,074
Yes sir.

91
00:06:23,814 --> 00:06:24,934
Well then, take good care of her.

92
00:06:26,014 --> 00:06:27,204
Thank you very much.

93
00:06:34,124 --> 00:06:35,424
How do you know him?

94
00:06:35,594 --> 00:06:36,584
Huh?

95
00:06:36,654 --> 00:06:37,784
That doctor. Who is he?

96
00:06:38,494 --> 00:06:41,264
He lives with Kohaku.

97
00:06:41,264 --> 00:06:42,234
Kohaku?

98
00:06:42,664 --> 00:06:44,394
Oh, that girl from the other day.

99
00:06:44,604 --> 00:06:45,894
Yes.

100
00:06:58,614 --> 00:06:59,774
What is it?

101
00:07:00,654 --> 00:07:04,314
Um... is Teacher Sayaka sick?

102
00:07:07,424 --> 00:07:08,654
She's okay.

103
00:07:08,754 --> 00:07:10,054
Really?

104
00:07:10,324 --> 00:07:13,764
Yeah. The doctor says she'll be fine in no time.

105
00:07:18,334 --> 00:07:21,794
If you put on long faces like that,
Ms. Sayaka is going to worry.

106
00:07:26,444 --> 00:07:30,404
Let's sing a song to help Ms. Sayaka feel better.

107
00:07:31,784 --> 00:07:32,974
Okay!

108
00:07:37,924 --> 00:07:42,784
I see blue, I see blue

109
00:07:42,994 --> 00:07:44,364
Looking up at the big, clear sky

110
00:07:44,364 --> 00:07:47,924
Kobato has completely forgotten about me.
Looking up at the big, clear sky

111
00:07:48,034 --> 00:07:53,094
As I feel, as I feel...

112
00:08:11,224 --> 00:08:12,284
Hey.

113
00:08:12,284 --> 00:08:13,344
Y-Yes.

114
00:08:13,824 --> 00:08:18,054
Is just sitting there doing nothing going
to make Ms. Sayaka better?

115
00:08:19,594 --> 00:08:21,664
But just for a little longer...

116
00:08:21,664 --> 00:08:22,964
Get over it already.

117
00:08:23,634 --> 00:08:27,034
She would have much more
peace of mind knowing

118
00:08:27,034 --> 00:08:31,234
that you were looking after the
children properly, wouldn't she?

119
00:08:34,774 --> 00:08:36,304
I guess you're right.

120
00:08:45,224 --> 00:08:46,444
How was it?

121
00:08:46,554 --> 00:08:48,324
How is the patient doing?

122
00:08:48,324 --> 00:08:49,554
Her symptoms have settled.

123
00:08:51,024 --> 00:08:53,294
Is that right? That's good to hear.

124
00:08:54,194 --> 00:08:59,154
And you go like this, and you
go like that, and see? A man!

125
00:09:00,774 --> 00:09:05,174
I get it. So that's how you play with origami.

126
00:09:07,814 --> 00:09:10,044
Look, look, Kobato.

127
00:09:10,584 --> 00:09:13,144
Wow, a balloon!

128
00:09:13,744 --> 00:09:16,014
Toshihiko, what are you folding?

129
00:09:16,484 --> 00:09:17,684
I'm folding cranes.

130
00:09:18,284 --> 00:09:19,274
Cranes?

131
00:09:19,554 --> 00:09:21,074
It's a type of bird.

132
00:09:22,454 --> 00:09:24,424
This is a bird, is it?

133
00:09:25,394 --> 00:09:27,054
You're folding so many.

134
00:09:27,434 --> 00:09:28,924
Mhm. One thousand!

135
00:09:29,134 --> 00:09:31,494
Huh? One thousand? That many?

136
00:09:31,804 --> 00:09:36,534
Yup. If I fold one-thousand cranes while
praying for Teacher Sayaka to get better,

137
00:09:36,534 --> 00:09:39,334
she's going to get better.

138
00:09:39,404 --> 00:09:40,564
Toshihiko!

139
00:09:40,944 --> 00:09:43,874
Can you show me how to fold this crane too?!

140
00:09:44,544 --> 00:09:45,784
I'll fold some too!

141
00:09:45,784 --> 00:09:47,184
I'm going to fold cranes too!

142
00:09:47,184 --> 00:09:48,214
Me too!

143
00:09:48,214 --> 00:09:50,314
Then let's all fold them together!

144
00:10:21,354 --> 00:10:23,874
I wonder if Kobato's all right.

145
00:10:24,824 --> 00:10:26,984
Shouldn't you be worrying about the patient?

146
00:10:27,124 --> 00:10:31,684
Oh of course. You're right. But...

147
00:10:32,994 --> 00:10:36,984
Why is it? For some reason, I can't
help but worry about Kobato.

148
00:10:43,974 --> 00:10:46,944
Will Teacher Sayaka be better by tomorrow?

149
00:10:46,944 --> 00:10:48,244
She'll be fine!

150
00:10:48,744 --> 00:10:50,834
Besides, we've folded one-thousand cranes!

151
00:10:51,884 --> 00:10:52,974
Mhm!

152
00:11:02,554 --> 00:11:05,754
I'll be back from work as soon as I can.

153
00:11:06,164 --> 00:11:08,634
You take good care of Ms. Sayaka.

154
00:11:09,434 --> 00:11:10,554
Yes.

155
00:11:11,964 --> 00:11:13,994
If anything happens, call me right away.

156
00:11:48,034 --> 00:11:50,504
Excuse me, I have a request.

157
00:11:50,704 --> 00:11:52,404
Seems serious. What is it?

158
00:11:53,644 --> 00:11:57,774
Would it be possible to cut
my hours back for awhile?

159
00:11:58,944 --> 00:12:00,754
I thought you needed the money.

160
00:12:00,754 --> 00:12:02,914
Well that's true, but...

161
00:12:04,254 --> 00:12:05,584
Right now I...

162
00:12:07,354 --> 00:12:08,884
Sure. No problem.

163
00:12:10,154 --> 00:12:13,564
But when you're back on track
I'm going to work you hard.

164
00:12:13,624 --> 00:12:15,964
Sorry for the inconvenience.
Thank you very much.

165
00:12:27,414 --> 00:12:28,934
Ms. Sayaka.

166
00:12:30,174 --> 00:12:31,574
Kobato?

167
00:12:33,244 --> 00:12:35,214
Were you here with me the whole time?

168
00:12:35,514 --> 00:12:36,784
Yes.

169
00:12:37,724 --> 00:12:39,054
What about the children?

170
00:12:39,054 --> 00:12:43,154
Their families came to pick them up
and they've all gone home.

171
00:12:43,654 --> 00:12:47,454
Oh. I'm so sorry to have worried you.

172
00:12:48,134 --> 00:12:49,964
No, don't get up yet. Please.

173
00:12:55,634 --> 00:12:57,794
I thought I had myself pulled together.

174
00:12:57,874 --> 00:12:58,844
Huh?

175
00:12:59,974 --> 00:13:03,634
With you helping out, I guess
somewhere I had let loose,

176
00:13:03,744 --> 00:13:07,734
knowing that I could count on you and Fujimoto.

177
00:13:12,354 --> 00:13:14,824
If something ever happens to me...

178
00:13:16,794 --> 00:13:18,724
What makes you say such a thing?!

179
00:13:19,864 --> 00:13:22,294
Don't... Don't even...

180
00:13:23,364 --> 00:13:25,994
I can't imagine something happening to you.

181
00:13:27,004 --> 00:13:31,834
That would make everyone too sad. So please...

182
00:13:32,874 --> 00:13:35,634
Don't ever say such a thing again!

183
00:13:41,814 --> 00:13:43,304
Kobato.

184
00:13:59,834 --> 00:14:01,924
You've helped enough. Go home now.

185
00:14:03,374 --> 00:14:04,304
Huh?

186
00:14:04,304 --> 00:14:06,394
You're clumsy as it is.

187
00:14:06,574 --> 00:14:10,274
I don't need you to become double clumsy
because you didn't get enough sleep.

188
00:14:10,274 --> 00:14:11,614
Double clumsy?!

189
00:14:11,744 --> 00:14:13,544
I'm not that clumsy!

190
00:14:13,644 --> 00:14:15,704
Just leave the rest to me and go home.

191
00:14:16,854 --> 00:14:18,144
Okay.

192
00:14:18,284 --> 00:14:20,124
Don't be clumsy and stumble on your way.

193
00:14:20,124 --> 00:14:21,354
I am not that bad.

194
00:14:21,354 --> 00:14:22,514
Just go.

195
00:14:28,794 --> 00:14:30,394
She scolded me.

196
00:14:30,964 --> 00:14:32,664
Good for her, considering.

197
00:14:33,404 --> 00:14:36,534
I guess so. Kobato is right.

198
00:14:38,244 --> 00:14:40,704
The children. They all folded.

199
00:14:41,374 --> 00:14:42,634
Is that so?

200
00:14:46,184 --> 00:14:47,914
This is a crane she folded.

201
00:14:48,314 --> 00:14:50,374
Agh, all these over here are hers.

202
00:14:53,084 --> 00:14:54,524
She's a good kid.

203
00:15:20,014 --> 00:15:22,484
Are you that worried about Sayaka?

204
00:15:24,454 --> 00:15:25,714
Hey Kobato.

205
00:15:26,624 --> 00:15:27,584
Huh?

206
00:15:30,024 --> 00:15:31,394
No, never mind.

207
00:15:31,764 --> 00:15:33,094
Okay.

208
00:15:36,734 --> 00:15:40,894
Could she be regaining that memory she lost?

209
00:15:42,234 --> 00:15:42,704
Hanamaro Drill
Language
"I did it!"
"It's fun!"

210
00:15:42,704 --> 00:15:44,604
Hanamaro Drill
Language
"I did it!"
"It's fun!"
Chiho, what's the answer to number seven?

211
00:15:44,604 --> 00:15:46,174
Chiho, what's the answer to number seven?

212
00:15:46,174 --> 00:15:48,604
What, Chise, don't you know either?

213
00:15:55,184 --> 00:15:56,114
Kobato.

214
00:15:56,114 --> 00:15:57,514
It's Kobato.

215
00:15:57,624 --> 00:16:00,384
Um... Is Ms. Chisato here?

216
00:16:00,384 --> 00:16:03,624
Mom's at a neighborhood meeting.

217
00:16:04,194 --> 00:16:05,494
Oh is that right?

218
00:16:05,894 --> 00:16:06,664
What's the matter?

219
00:16:06,664 --> 00:16:08,394
You look sad, Kobato.

220
00:16:08,894 --> 00:16:10,034
Actually...

221
00:16:10,034 --> 00:16:11,224
I'm worried about an illness!

222
00:16:13,504 --> 00:16:14,864
Oh no, Kobato!

223
00:16:21,144 --> 00:16:24,234
No, no, no, not me!

224
00:16:24,644 --> 00:16:25,674
Huh?

225
00:16:26,014 --> 00:16:28,814
Ms. Sayaka is sick.

226
00:16:32,884 --> 00:16:38,294
I want to do something for her,
but I don't know what to do?

227
00:16:39,964 --> 00:16:43,664
I tried folding one-thousand
cranes with everybody.

228
00:16:43,664 --> 00:16:45,134
One-thousand cranes.

229
00:16:45,134 --> 00:16:46,194
Yes.

230
00:16:46,534 --> 00:16:52,644
But I couldn't fold them very well and I'm
afraid that because of my poor folding,

231
00:16:52,644 --> 00:16:54,104
our wish won't come true.

232
00:16:54,744 --> 00:16:56,504
Don't worry, Kobato.

233
00:16:56,714 --> 00:16:59,344
I'm certain that your wish will come true.

234
00:17:01,054 --> 00:17:02,954
I certainly hope so.

235
00:17:04,724 --> 00:17:06,154
Oh, how about that?

236
00:17:06,324 --> 00:17:09,684
You know, when we're sick,
Mom always makes it for us.

237
00:17:11,264 --> 00:17:12,264
Rice porridge...

238
00:17:12,264 --> 00:17:13,624
That's right, rice porridge.

239
00:17:13,694 --> 00:17:15,094
Of course, rice porridge

240
00:17:16,434 --> 00:17:18,934
Mom says porridge is easy to digest,

241
00:17:18,934 --> 00:17:21,234
so it's not too hard on your
stomach even when you're sick.

242
00:17:21,574 --> 00:17:23,124
Easy to digest?

243
00:17:23,204 --> 00:17:25,464
Come to think of it,
Shuichiro said the same thing.

244
00:17:25,704 --> 00:17:29,074
To give Ms. Sayaka something that digests well.

245
00:17:29,274 --> 00:17:31,974
Then Kobato, make her some rice porridge.

246
00:17:32,044 --> 00:17:34,784
Mhm. That will make Ms. Sayaka better for sure.

247
00:17:34,784 --> 00:17:37,914
Yes! I will make rice porridge for Ms. Sayaka!

248
00:17:39,454 --> 00:17:41,654
But how do I make rice porridge?

249
00:17:41,724 --> 00:17:44,194
I know. Chiho, why don't you draw a picture?

250
00:17:44,194 --> 00:17:45,994
Great idea, Chise!

251
00:17:49,294 --> 00:17:51,064
It looks kind of like this.

252
00:17:51,664 --> 00:17:53,824
This is rice porridge?

253
00:17:54,234 --> 00:17:55,674
It's white and...

254
00:17:55,674 --> 00:17:57,874
Kind of gooey, I think.

255
00:17:57,874 --> 00:18:00,574
That's right. It's gooey!

256
00:18:00,574 --> 00:18:01,114
Gooey
That's right. It's gooey!

257
00:18:01,114 --> 00:18:01,804
Gooey

258
00:18:02,144 --> 00:18:06,514
Oh and when we eat it, Mom would tell us,
"be careful or you'll burn your tongue".

259
00:18:06,644 --> 00:18:08,614
Very hot!

260
00:18:08,614 --> 00:18:12,554
And when she made it she
would add lots of water.

261
00:18:12,754 --> 00:18:15,184
Full of water!

262
00:18:15,424 --> 00:18:15,954
Amazing.

263
00:18:15,954 --> 00:18:17,594
I have an uneasy feeling about this.
Amazing.

264
00:18:17,594 --> 00:18:18,214
I have an uneasy feeling about this.

265
00:18:57,294 --> 00:18:58,264
Who is it?!

266
00:19:04,874 --> 00:19:06,234
What are you doing?!

267
00:19:07,144 --> 00:19:10,234
I was trying... to make rice porridge.

268
00:19:11,484 --> 00:19:12,014
Very hot
How to make rice porridge
White
Easy to digest
Gooey

269
00:19:12,014 --> 00:19:16,084
Very hot
How to make rice porridge
White
Easy to digest
Gooey
After all that effort Chiho and Chise
made to show me how...

270
00:19:16,084 --> 00:19:16,414
Very hot
How to make rice porridge
White
Easy to digest
Gooey

271
00:19:16,914 --> 00:19:18,644
and I couldn't get it right.

272
00:19:20,024 --> 00:19:22,324
Apparently rice porridge is
good for the digestion.

273
00:19:23,154 --> 00:19:25,384
That's why I thought Ms. Sayaka...

274
00:19:30,394 --> 00:19:33,694
First, you wash the rice you'll use,
and then add lots of water.

275
00:19:34,234 --> 00:19:36,894
Put it over the heat until it boils.

276
00:19:38,004 --> 00:19:40,034
After that, let it stew over low heat. That's it.

277
00:19:41,174 --> 00:19:44,614
How in the world do you come
up with that concoction?

278
00:19:46,084 --> 00:19:49,484
Feed her something like that
and she'll just get worse.

279
00:19:57,354 --> 00:19:59,794
C-Come on, don't cry.

280
00:20:00,624 --> 00:20:03,594
If Ms. Sayaka dies...

281
00:20:09,534 --> 00:20:12,774
Don't worry. People don't die that easily.

282
00:20:12,774 --> 00:20:14,604
Sometimes they do!

283
00:20:18,584 --> 00:20:23,044
Sometimes it doesn't take very
much for someone to die.

284
00:20:25,954 --> 00:20:27,714
Did that happen to someone you know?

285
00:20:33,424 --> 00:20:34,654
It's all right.

286
00:20:35,634 --> 00:20:37,694
Ms. Sayaka is not going to die.

287
00:20:49,474 --> 00:20:50,534
It's okay.

288
00:20:57,684 --> 00:21:00,914
Oh this is good! I'll be a hundred times better!

289
00:21:02,124 --> 00:21:03,524
I'm glad!

290
00:21:03,894 --> 00:21:05,584
But I might end up eating too much.

291
00:21:06,964 --> 00:21:08,254
Mmm, delicious.

292
00:21:08,894 --> 00:21:10,954
I'm glad I could be of some help.

293
00:21:11,234 --> 00:21:13,794
Although I actually did most of the cooking.

294
00:21:14,404 --> 00:21:16,734
W-Well that's true, but...

295
00:21:16,734 --> 00:21:17,964
But what?

296
00:21:18,544 --> 00:21:20,444
Nothing at all.

297
00:21:20,644 --> 00:21:21,764
I didn't think so.

298
00:21:30,154 --> 00:21:31,674
It's not like there are any more than there were.

299
00:21:32,554 --> 00:21:36,084
You don't get more kompeito by
just looking at them, you know!

300
00:21:36,224 --> 00:21:37,414
Yes!

301
00:21:38,994 --> 00:21:41,054
But you're not upset.

302
00:21:41,434 --> 00:21:42,824
Come to think of it...

303
00:21:44,394 --> 00:21:45,794
I wonder why.

304
00:21:48,404 --> 00:21:49,634
When I cried...

305
00:21:50,104 --> 00:21:53,344
When I cried as hard as I could
in front of Fujimoto...

306
00:21:53,344 --> 00:21:58,644
It was as if this heaviness in
my heart lightened up,

307
00:22:00,344 --> 00:22:03,214
and I was left with this very warm feeling.

308
00:22:05,654 --> 00:22:09,614
So what now? You're supposed to be healing
others but you're letting others heal you.

309
00:22:11,624 --> 00:22:13,064
Heal me?

310
00:22:15,664 --> 00:22:17,754
Is this what?

311
00:22:19,964 --> 00:22:25,434
Good morning!

312
00:22:26,004 --> 00:22:27,274
Morning.

313
00:22:27,274 --> 00:22:28,674
It's Teacher Sayaka!

314
00:22:28,974 --> 00:22:29,874
Good morning!

315
00:22:29,874 --> 00:22:31,884
Good morning, Teacher Sayaka!

316
00:22:31,884 --> 00:22:32,784
Good morning.

317
00:22:32,784 --> 00:22:34,714
Are you all better now?

318
00:22:35,054 --> 00:22:36,614
I'm all better now.

319
00:22:36,614 --> 00:22:39,144
So the thousand cranes worked?

320
00:22:39,854 --> 00:22:41,654
Good morning, Kobato!

321
00:22:41,894 --> 00:22:44,254
Yes! Good morning!

322
00:23:01,344 --> 00:23:08,974
Everyone dreams of flying

323
00:23:10,154 --> 00:23:16,254
But they let gravity trick them

324
00:23:16,524 --> 00:23:24,364
Honestly, everyone is already able to fly

325
00:23:26,604 --> 00:23:32,934
I bet the reason that child looks so terribly sad

326
00:23:33,974 --> 00:23:36,844
Is because he

327
00:23:36,844 --> 00:23:43,974
Accidentally lost his shadow somewhere

328
00:23:44,154 --> 00:23:46,674
In that case

329
00:23:46,854 --> 00:23:50,954
If I could just tell you, "Thank you,"

330
00:23:50,954 --> 00:23:54,834
And you laugh and reply, "Thank you"

331
00:23:54,834 --> 00:24:02,164
That exchange would fill you with joy

332
00:24:02,704 --> 00:24:06,934
It would make you feel so happy

333
00:24:07,244 --> 00:24:11,484
There's nothing to worry about

334
00:24:11,484 --> 00:24:15,574
Since we're together

335
00:24:17,354 --> 00:24:23,294
It's strange how I'm crying

336
00:24:23,294 --> 00:24:26,064
Even though I'm happy

337
00:24:26,064 --> 00:24:29,034
Next episode
...Mysterious Life Form.
Even though I'm happy

338
00:24:29,034 --> 00:24:30,754
Next episode
...Mysterious Life Form.

